Quetzalcoatl was originally the Titan of the [[elder daughter of Casterwill]] who stored its Ring inside the [[Willblade]], a powerful weapon that she had forged. {{Source|S2E50}} [[Pendragon|Pendragon's]] Amulet eventually took the place of that of Quetzalcoatl inside the Willblade, {{Source|S2E30}} and Quetzalcoatl's Ring was sealed by itself in the [[Pyramid of the Sun]], a temple dedicated to the Titan in the Aztec capital of [[Teotihuacan, Mexico]]. {{Source|S2E38}} 

In the modern age, the Huntik team were sent on a mission by [[Teien Casterwill]] to activate the Blue Star to call the Casterwills out of hiding. After reaching the Pyramid of the Sun, [[Lok Lambert]] managed to awaken Quetzalcoatl when Den ignited the blue powder stored within the temple. After scaring off [[Kiel]] and his [[Blood Spiral]]s, Quetzalcoatl rose into the sky to become the Blue Star, summing together the members of the [[Casterwill family]] against the [[Blood Spiral]]. {{source|The Titan in the Temple of Sun}}

In [[Tír na nÓg]], Lok's father [[Eathon]] told him that Pendragon might not be enough to defeat the Spiral, and that Lok would need something else. The Blue Star of Quetzalcoatl then briefly appeared. {{source|Back Home}} 

After heeding his father's words, Lok later managed to summon back Quetzalcoatl from the [[Blue Star]] form to use in battle against [[the Betrayer]]. After manifesting Quetzalcoatl's Ring in his hand, Lok placed it back in the [[Willblade]] and used it to to defeat [[Demigorgan]], the Titan of Betrayal, and destroy his [[Amulet]] for good. {{source|Dante's Return}}.
